<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Apr non-CIS nickel exports up 37 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Apr non-CIS nickel exports up 37 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 67,400 tonnes of nickel outside the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) over January-April, up 37 percent on year-ago levels and a continuation of the strong deliveries seen so far this year, the State Statistics Committee said Thursday.</p>
<p>Non-CIS aluminium exports were up two percent year-on-year during the first four months to 880,000 tonnes. The committee gave the following data --  </p>
<p>RUSSIAN JAN-APRIL NON-CIS NON-FERROUS METAL EXPORTS (TONNES)</p>
<p>				Jan-April	  pct change on</p>
<p>				  1997	     Jan-April 1996</p>
<p> aluminium		   880,000		  +2</p>
<p> copper			183,000		  +8</p>
<p> nickel			 67,400		 +37</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
